  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The paper focuses on the conceptual and technical design of the portal rather than empirical testing of its effectiveness on public behavior during an actual disaster.",
      "what": "This paper presents the conceptual and technical framework of Germany's Natural Hazards Portal (Naturgefahrenportal, NGP), a platform designed to consolidate and standardise fragmented hazard warnings and maps from various federal and state authorities. The system harmonises warning levels, terminology, and colour codes into a unified visual interface to resolve inconsistencies across different agency outputs.",
      "why": "It establishes a unified national communication standard for multi-hazard warnings, replacing a fragmented system of agency-specific portals that confused the public and hindered rapid, accurate emergency responses."
    }
